-- title:
--   Unramified Gauss-type valuation ring on the prime-to-q level field
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $\pi_0\in k_0$ have image in $A$, and write $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$; assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, has algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Let $\ell'$ be a prime with $\ell'\ne q$, $\ell'\ge 3$, $\ell'\nmid M'$, let $\xi\in k_0$ be a primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity, and assume some ring homomorphism $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K''$ be the intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq k_0((X))$ generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(\ell'^2M')$, where $H\le(\mathbb Z/\ell'^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell')^\times$, and equip $K''$ with an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with the tower $A_0\to k_0\to K''$. Let $j''\in K''$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion of $j$, and assume $j''\ne0$. Then there is a valuation subring $V$ of $K''$ such that: the image of every element of $A_0$ lies in $V$; the image of $\pi_0$ is a non-unit of $V$; for every polynomial $P$ over $A_0$ not divisible by the constant $\pi_0$, both $P(j'')$ and $P(j'')^{-1}$ lie in $V$; and every non-unit $f$ of $V$ satisfies $f\cdot\pi_0^{-1}\in V$.
--
--   This is the existence of the Gauss (coefficientwise) valuation ring on the level-$\ell'^2M'$ modular function field over $k_0$, characterised by being of Gauss type relative to $j''$ and unramified over $A_0$ in the sense that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$. It feeds the analysis of the fibre of the modular curve of level prime to $q$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_isPrime_chartAlgFin_of_coprime_level`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_isPrime_chartAlgFin_of_coprime_level); the valuation ring is produced from the regular prolongation of $A_0$ along the Laurent base change of the $q$-expansion function field, together with the transcendence of the $q$-expansion parameter.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_valuationSubring_gaussType_unramified_of_coprime_level.lean

